{
  "decision": "NO_CHANGE",
  "workflow_yaml": null,
  "rationale": "The workflow already implements the applicable evidence-supported optimizations. Path-based change filtering is present via the `changes` job with `AurorNZ/paths-filter` (P-LIT-CHANGE-FILTER). Superseded-run cancellation is already configured via `concurrency` with `cancel-in-progress: true` (P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE). Dependency caching is already present for npm (`setup-node` with `cache: npm` and `cache-dependency-path: web/package-lock.json`) and Cargo (`Swatinem/rust-cache@v2`) (P-LIT-GHA-CACHE). The remaining candidate patterns are not safely applicable: P-LIT-FAIL-FAST (setting `fail-fast: true`) is contraindicated because every matrix outcome is required for cross-platform (Node 24/26 × ubuntu/windows) and cross-browser (chrome/firefox/edge) coverage; P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT lacks representative per-job successful-duration history (only workflow-level run times are available in ci_history) and valid slow Rust/wasm/browser-test runs could exceed an arbitrary limit, causing false timeouts. No additional cacheable dependency source is identified beyond the existing npm and Cargo caches.",
  "evidence_ids": ["P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "P-LIT-CANCEL-STALE", "P-LIT-CHANGE-FILTER", "P-LIT-FAIL-FAST", "P-LIT-CUSTOM-TIMEOUT"]
}
